Docbank keeps documents in a local vault: a virtual folder tree (/cases/a.pdf)
over immutable, hash-verified content versions. A background daemon owns the
vault; data commands start it automatically ("docbank daemon stop" ends it).

DOCBANK_HOME selects the vault (default ~/.docbank); the first data command
creates it. "docbank info --json" confirms its path and identity. Local data
commands use that vault; push --to selects an explicit remote daemon instead.

Agent workflow (replace example paths and ids with your own):
  docbank info --json                         # 1. confirm the selected vault
  docbank add ./scans --dest /cases/acme       # 2. import (creates folders)
  docbank tree /cases --json                  # 3. browse paths and ids
  docbank search invoice 2026 --agent         # 4. find by name or text
  docbank stat id:12 --json                   # 5. read current_version_id
  docbank cat /cases/acme/notes.txt            # 6. read original bytes
  docbank get id:12 ./invoice.pdf             # 7. save a verified copy
  docbank backup init --repo ~/backup         # 8. initialize a separate repo
  docbank backup create --repo ~/backup       # 9. capture a snapshot

Concepts:
  path-or-id  a node is "/abs/path" or "id:N"; id:N survives mv and rename
  version     put/edit add an immutable version (UUID); revert restores one
  text        search reads text/*, JSON and email bodies; PDFs and Office
              files need a processing profile (see "docbank processing")
  rendition   derived Markdown text made by a processing profile
  deletion    rm -> trash empty -> gc -> storage repack; each step is explicit

Output: results on stdout; errors, recovery hints and progress on stderr.
Use --json where listed in command help; search --agent gives compact hit rows.
With parsed --json, failures end with a JSON stderr record containing
error.message, error.code, error.exit and error.hint (when present).
Existing previews/progress may precede it. Flag parsing can fail before --json
is read; those errors stay human text. Human hints use hint:; agent uses Hint:.

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 operational/internal error, 2 usage or request validation,
3 not found, 4 stale revision, 5 busy/locked, 6 integrity, 7 claim required.

Environment: DOCBANK_HOME selects vault data and config.toml.
Daemon startup overrides (restart the daemon after changing them):
  DOCBANK_BIND_ADDR bind IP (default loopback); DOCBANK_API_PORT API port
  DOCBANK_API_KEY or DOCBANK_API_KEY_FILE configured key (choose only one)
  DOCBANK_ALLOWED_HOSTS comma-separated HTTP Host allowlist
Without a configured key, the daemon generates a private per-run key.

Usage:
  docbank [command]

Documents:
  add  Import files or directory trees into the vault
  cat  Print a file's original bytes to stdout
  edit  Edit a file through a new immutable content version
  get  Download one file with end-to-end verification
  ls  List one virtual directory (default /)
  mkdir  Create a directory in the virtual tree
  mv  Move or rename a node (metadata only; bytes never move)
  provenance  Show where a document came from
  put  Replace a file's content while retaining its immutable history
  refs  Find document versions that retain a content hash
  restore  Restore a trashed node to its original location
  revert  Create a new current version from an immutable prior version
  rm  Move a node (and its subtree) to the trash
  stat  Inspect one document or directory
  tag  Define tags and organize nodes with them
  trash  Inspect and empty the trash
  tree  Print the virtual folder tree with id:N selectors
  versions  Inspect and maintain immutable content versions

Search and text:
  formats  Report per-format capability coverage
  processing  Preview and run document processing
  rendition  Read retained document renditions
  search  Find files and folders by name, text, tag, type, folder, or date
  search-export  Export search counts and review saved evidence

Email, media, photos, people:
  email-documents  Inspect and release email attachment relationships
  email-pdf  Render and download one exact email version as a verified PDF
  mailbox  Import verified MBOX, Takeout ZIP, or explicitly identified EML
  media  Retain and inspect recordings
  people  Manage canonical people
  photos  Manage photo assets
  push  Push a local folder to a remote daemon
  watch  Inspect configured watched inboxes

Exports and productions:
  bates  Plan and reserve Bates labels for exported PDFs
  export  Export originals or rendered photos as verified ZIP bundles
  labels  Look up package-scoped received and assigned labels
  package  Inspect and exchange load-file packages
  redaction  Review and redact retained PDFs
  transfer  Inspect portable transfer packages

Vault operations:
  audit  Protect permanent document history and inspect its evidence
  backup  Create, restore, and clean up vault snapshots
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  daemon  Manage the docbank daemon
  gc  Reclaim unreachable blobs (dry-run unless --run)
  help  Help about any command
  info  Identify the selected vault and summarize its contents
  jobs  List daemon background workers and storage operations
  storage  Inspect and maintain physical blob storage
  update  Update docbank to the latest GitHub release
  verify  Validate metadata and re-hash every stored blob
  version  Print the installed Docbank version

Interfaces:
  kata  Quote document passages in Kata issues
  mcp  Serve the local vault over Model Context Protocol
  openapi  Print the HTTP API's OpenAPI YAML document (no daemon needed)
  tui  Browse and search the vault interactively
  web  Open the local web application

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for docbank

Use "docbank [command] --help" for more information about a command.
